{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevAsymptotic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.KashaevAsymptotic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.LobNearZero","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.StirlingRobbins"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaev_log_sum_asymptotic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaev_log_sum_asymptotic","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevAsymptotic.lean#L109-L270","doc":"**The assembly.**  `∑_{j=1}^{k} log(2 sin(jπ/N))` equals\n`−(N/π)Λ(θ) + ½log(2N sin θ) + (π/12N)cot θ` up to `O(1/N²)`, with an explicit\nconstant.  See the file header for the five pieces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_robbins_centred","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_robbins_centred","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevAsymptotic.lean#L62-L85","doc":"**Robbins, centred.**  `log k! − (k log k − k + ½log k + ½log 2π)` sits\nwithin `1/(144k²)` of `1/(12k)`.  Both Robbins inequalities are needed: the\n`1/(12k)` is not an error term here, it CANCELS against `(h/12)·(1/θ)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}